# core:data Conventions

## Repository Implementation

```kotlin
class TransactionRepositoryImpl @Inject constructor(
    private val localDataSource: TransactionLocalDataSource,
    private val firestoreDataSource: TransactionFirestoreDataSource,
    private val mapper: TransactionMapper,
) : TransactionRepository {

    override fun observeTransactions(): Flow<List<Transaction>> =
        localDataSource.observeAll().map { entities ->
            entities.map(mapper::toDomain)
        }

    override suspend fun addTransaction(transaction: Transaction) {
        localDataSource.insert(mapper.toEntity(transaction))
    }
}
```

Rules:
- `@Inject constructor` — always constructor-injected
- Implements interface from `:core:domain`
- All reads come from local source (Room) — offline-first pattern
- Writes go to local first, then sync to Firestore via WorkManager
- Handle `CancellationException` properly:

```kotlin
// ✅ Correct
try { ... } catch (e: CancellationException) { throw e } catch (e: Exception) { handleError(e) }

// ❌ Wrong — swallows cancellation
try { ... } catch (e: Exception) { handleError(e) }
```

## Data Source

- Interface in `datasource/` — implementation in same package with `Impl` suffix
- Firestore data sources: use `companion object` for collection/field constants
- Local data sources: wrap Room DAO calls

```kotlin
// Firestore constants pattern
private companion object {
    const val COLLECTION_TRANSACTIONS = "transactions"
    const val FIELD_USER_ID = "userId"
    const val FIELD_AMOUNT = "amount"
}
```

## Mapper

```kotlin
class TransactionMapper @Inject constructor() {
    fun toDomain(entity: TransactionEntity): Transaction = Transaction(...)
    fun toEntity(domain: Transaction): TransactionEntity = TransactionEntity(...)
}
```

Rules:
- Separate class — not extension functions on entities
- Bidirectional: `toDomain()` and `toEntity()`/`toResponse()`
- `@Inject constructor` for Hilt provision (or provide via `@Module`)

## DI Module

```kotlin
@Module
@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
interface RepositoryModule {
    @Binds
    fun bindTransactionRepository(impl: TransactionRepositoryImpl): TransactionRepository
}
```

Rules:
- Use `@Binds` for interface→impl bindings (not `@Provides`)
- Use `@Provides` only for third-party instances (Firebase, Room DB)
- Install in `SingletonComponent` for app-scoped singletons
- One module per concern: `RepositoryModule`, `DataSourceModule`, `MapperModule`, `DatabaseModule`
